# Database & Security (Critical)

## Stack

- Prefer **Prisma + PostgreSQL** when introducing persistence. If the repo later chooses differently, update this rule and `AGENTS.md`—do not run two ORMs.
- Use safe Prisma/query APIs; never concatenate untrusted input into raw SQL. Parameterize any raw queries.

## Authorization

- Enforce **workspace-level access control** on every protected operation (reads and writes).
- Never trust client-supplied `workspaceId` (or similar) without verifying membership/role server-side.
- Return safe auth errors (401/403) without leaking whether a resource exists across workspaces.

## Secrets and data handling

- Never expose secrets, API keys, or DB credentials to browser bundles; use server-only env vars.
- Do not log passwords, tokens, session secrets, or unnecessary PII.
- Treat uploads and imported content as untrusted (size limits, type checks, no blind eval of CSV formulas).

## Data integrity

- Add database constraints and indexes where appropriate (unique import keys, FKs, workspace-scoped uniqueness).
- Use transactions for multi-step financial and inventory changes.
- Protect against duplicate imports and repeated idempotent operations (idempotency keys / unique constraints).
- Maintain audit logs for important financial and inventory mutations.

## Development hygiene

- Do not weaken auth, RLS/workspace checks, or secret handling to make local development easier.
- Handle auth failures explicitly; never catch-and-ignore authorization errors.
